PATCH 517: five more cockpit glyph plates emitted as a bare arg-less `lcall [0x6b4]`.

An image-wide scan for the exact shape
    mov di,[0x6d34] ; movzbw ax,[di+0x3f] ; add ax,K ; mov bx,B ; lcall [0x6b4]
finds seven sites; two (0x81e6, 0x81f8) were already fixed by patch 504.  The remaining five:

    0x73d4  K=0x1470  B=0x8dcc      FUN_0000_73d4
    0x787d  K=0x0380  B=0x8eee      FUN_0000_787d
    0x8bfb  K=0x0838  B=0x9176  \
    0x8c0d  K=0x0848  B=0x917e   >  FUN_0000_8bfb, two plates in one function
    0x8dc6  K=0x07d8  B=0x916e      FUN_0000_8dc6

DAT_2000_2d34 holds the PLAYER's NEAR OFFSET (patch 300).  Ghidra emitted every one of these as a body
containing nothing but `(*(code *)fist_icall_far(DAT_1000_c6b4))();` -- no player lookup, no glyph id, no
BX -- so the paint service ran on whatever AX and BX happened to hold at the call.

787d is the one that matters most right now: it is dispatched by the 209e dirty walk, so after patch 513
it received the walk's real AX (on the first mission frame that is the tick counter) as its glyph id and
still no BX, and it feeds FUN_0000_26a1 -> FUN_0000_260c, whose clip outputs at DGROUP:0x1586..0x158f are
the native<->wasm RENDER divergence the extended fingerprint reports at t=274, the first in-mission tick
(watchpointed: 260c <- 26a1 <- 787d <- 209e <- 206f <- 459a).
--- a/fist.c
+++ b/fist.c
@@ -19681,7 +19681,15 @@
 void __allregs FUN_0000_73d4(void)
 
 {
-  (*(code *)fist_icall_far((uint32_t)(DAT_1000_c6b4)))();
+  /* PATCH 517: a cockpit glyph plate (asm 0x73d4-0x73e6):
+   *     mov di,[0x6d34] ; movzbw ax,[di+0x3f] ; add ax,0x1470 ; mov bx,0x8dcc ; lcall [0x6b4]
+   * DAT_2000_2d34 is the PLAYER's NEAR OFFSET (patch 300).  Ghidra emitted the whole body as a bare
+   * arg-less `lcall [0x6b4]` -- no player lookup, no glyph id, no BX -- so the paint service ran on
+   * whatever AX and BX happened to hold. */
+  unsigned char *dg = (unsigned char *)g_mem + 0x1c000;
+  unsigned short di = (unsigned short)DAT_2000_2d34;
+  (*(code *)fist_icall_far((uint32_t)(DAT_1000_c6b4)))
+      ((unsigned short)(dg[(unsigned short)(di + 0x3f)] + 0x1470),0x8dcc);
   return;
 }
 
